    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0837" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg737"/>

                <head>No. 466.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 1, 1880</date>.
                        (Received March 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1108.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: During the suspension of diplomatic
                    relations between Mexico and Belgium, it has been the practice of this legation
                    and the consulate in Mexico, when proper occasion required, to extend their good
                    offices to Belgian residents in this country.</p>
                <p>These relations having been recently restored, the Belgian minister
                    plenipotentiary near this government has sent me a note, of which I inclose a
                    translation, expressing to our government the gratitude of His Majesty’s
                    government for these services.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d466-a1.xml" xpointer="d466-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
